1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,119
<i>You can formally</i>
<i>introduce yourselves later.</i>

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,680
This is Phatee.
He'll be A-Team's main vocalist.

3
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,320
<i>Good.</i>

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,480
Let's make this the debut song.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,160
Thanks for working so hard.
For doing something you're not good at.

6
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,960
I'll be right by your side.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,160
<i>And I'll push you forward.</i>

8
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,400
<i>You've always been an inspiration to me.</i>

9
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,119
<i>Did you know me before?</i>

10
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:46,720
RANNE

11
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,680
How did you get in?

12
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,680
Well, was it your friend?

13
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:16,480
The one named Tangmo.

14
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,480
He told me to wait up here.

15
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,840
We went to the same school.

16
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:33,000
You never told me.

17
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,440
Is that why you knew I was your senior?

18
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,240
No.

19
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,680
I don't remember either.

20
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,480
Really?

21
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,720
Really.

22
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,920
It was a long time ago.

23
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,280
Then why…

24
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,600
did you give me flowers back then?

25
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,600
This looks like the handwriting
of someone who gave me flowers.

26
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,840
You don't give flowers
to everyone, do you?

27
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:30,600
Why did you give me flowers
and then disappear?

28
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,000
It was a long time ago.

29
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,560
I think you've got me confused
with someone else.

30
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,280
Do you like me?

31
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:48,560
This is getting out of hand.

32
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,840
You've got it wrong.

33
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,440
I've never liked you.

34
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,400
So…

35
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,120
Why are you here?

36
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,560
I was worried about you.

37
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,320
You just disappeared.

38
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,560
I couldn't reach you.

39
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:10,160
So I came to see you.

40
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,440
Do you guys really think it'll work?

41
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,200
Tomorrow's the deadline Kao gave us.

42
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,400
Hey.

43
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,440
If we don't try, we'll never know, right?

44
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,960
Where's Phatee? Why isn't he here?

45
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,560
You guys carry on for me.

46
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,880
Okay.

47
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,560
Phatee, is something wrong?

48
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,120
Saw won't come back

49
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,360
if you keep using AI songs.

50
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,240
Stop using AI.

51
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,720
I can't.

52
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,320
The song's already finalized.

53
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,680
And… if Saw doesn't come back,

54
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:11,920
the four of you can debut.

55
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:16,320
I can't sing a song written by AI either.

56
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,720
It doesn't have the same meaning
as one written by a real person.

57
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,280
What do you mean?

58
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:22,600
If the band doesn't have you,

59
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,440
I'll have to disband it.

60
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:32,120
I really can't escape you guys.

61
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,920
Whoa, Saw!

62
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,560
I missed you.
Where have you been for days?

63
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,760
Miss you, Bro.

64
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,400
Miss you, Bro.

65
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,600
You're overdoing it, farang.
It's only been a few days.

66
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,480
And you're acting like… Jeez.

67
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,800
You call me farang? Look at yourself.

68
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,760
You both look fucking farang.

69
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,160
Got you there.

70
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,520
How did you guys know I was here?

71
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,880
Phatee, huh?

72
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,120
If we hadn't come all
the way here for you,

73
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,880
would you have come back?

74
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,800
Just because you came

75
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:11,560
doesn't mean I'm going back.

76
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,960
Besides,

77
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,600
no matter what,
Kao doesn't care about me anyway.

78
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:27,560
She only cares about you and Phatee.

79
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,160
Hey, Saw.

80
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,880
How could Kao not care about you?

81
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,120
She cares about all of us.

82
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,160
And even if she really
doesn't care about you,

83
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:39,080
fuck it.

84
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,560
Everyone here

85
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,880
cares about you.

86
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,520
I don't know.

87
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,720
if Kao still uses AI songs,

88
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,680
I'm out.

89
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:53,040
Even if I go back,
you'll still use AI songs.

90
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,960
That's definitely not happening.

91
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,000
Otherwise, why would I come all
the way here?

92
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,360
I'll give you the freedom
to make your music.

93
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:04,480
I won't let AI interfere
with your work again.

94
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,440
I promise.

95
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,280
Trust me.

96
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,600
I understand you guys now.

97
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,200
If you mean it,

98
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,960
I'm okay with it.

99
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,720
Yes!

100
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:31,960
You'd better mean it.

101
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:34,280
But I'm not postponing your debut.

102
00:08:34,799 --> 00:08:37,159
Hurry and practice for the debut stage.

103
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,840
Sure.

104
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:41,559
Piece of cake.

105
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:51,760
Come on, you guys. Hug it out.

106
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:54,960
You're happy, aren't you? Come on.

107
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:59,080
You need to practice
when you get back, Saw.

108
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:15,160
<i>Oh-ooh-woah, can I whisper it softly?</i>

109
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:19,400
<i>Can I whisper it softly to your ear</i>

110
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:22,400
<i>That I love you?</i>

111
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,680
How is it, guys?
Anything you want to change?

112
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,920
- I'm good with it.
- It's good.

113
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,040
And for our debut song,

114
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,120
do we need to dance to
show people it's danceable?

115
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:40,240
This song focuses on vocals. Let's try…

116
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:42,640
moving between positions
and entertaining the crowd instead.

117
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:45,400
For the hook, we'll find
some easy-to-remember moves.

118
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,040
What do you guys think?

119
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:52,280
- Let's try it.
- Okay.

120
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,240
Then…

121
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,280
let's do what Phatee said.

122
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,120
Wow, when you talk to Phatee,

123
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,720
your voice is so sweet.

124
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,160
But when you talk to us…

125
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:05,840
True. Phatee too.

126
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:07,000
He's so different

127
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,280
when he talks to Ranne.

128
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,200
You guys are acting suspicious.

129
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:13,960
I've been gone for three days.
Did I miss something?

130
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:17,160
Knock it off. You know why?

131
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:20,280
Because Phatee isn't rude to
me like you guys are.

132
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,320
All right, keep practicing.

133
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,480
Okay, don't get mad to cover it up.

134
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,720
I'm not mad.

135
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,120
Come on. Let's practice.

136
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:39,120
If this band doesn't have you,

137
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,200
I'll have to disband it.

138
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,600
And if I agree to work
as a pair with Ranne,

139
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:48,280
will you let us write our own songs again?

140
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:07,040
From now on,
post behind-the-scenes rehearsal clips

141
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:09,200
of Phatee and Ranne every day.

142
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,640
Keep it natural. Don't push it too hard.

143
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:16,000
If the fans like it,
they'll hype them up themselves.

144
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,520
Kao.

145
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:23,000
I wanted to tell you that
our channel right now,

146
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,720
especially the clips of Phatee and Ranne,

147
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:27,480
are getting millions of views.

148
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,800
More views than any other member.

149
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,320
If being a group causes so many problems,

150
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,240
why not debut these two as a duo?

151
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,800
Phatee and Ranne won't agree to that.

152
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,720
Besides,

153
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:43,040
if we're going to make someone stand out,

154
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:45,000
we need some supporting players.

155
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:51,000
Want a drink? I'm about to order.

156
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,160
No, thanks. Go ahead.

157
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,800
Where are the others?

158
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:58,760
PJ and Tonhon took
Phatee over there to film a TikTok.

159
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,400
So…

160
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,120
what's going on with you and Phatee?

161
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,080
Are you two flirting?

162
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:09,520
What flirting?

163
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,880
He's just a junior in the band.

164
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:14,640
I believe you don't feel anything.

165
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,360
It's just content.

166
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,520
Kao's pushing you two anyway.

167
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,720
But Phatee?

168
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,240
I'm not so sure.

169
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,280
I think he seems normal.

170
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,120
How does he seem normal?

171
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,880
The way he looks at you

172
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,640
isn't how he looks at other people.

173
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,440
He seems to care about you a lot.

174
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:43,560
- Really?
- Yeah.

175
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,360
How do you feel about him?

176
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,400
Well…

177
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,040
he's pretty cute.

178
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:01,840
Nice smile.

179
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,360
Good at guitar.

180
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,920
And he sings well.

181
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,520
But he's a bit too private.

182
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,240
Still, I don't know why.

183
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:15,680
When I'm with him, I feel comfortable.

184
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,800
Do you like him?

185
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:25,000
He's okay. He's a sweet little brother.

186
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,880
What about as a boyfriend?

187
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:39,400
RANNE

188
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,120
Hey, perfect timing.

189
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:49,680
Tonhon, PJ, come here.

190
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,440
- What?
- I'm about to order drinks.

191
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,920
What do you guys want?

192
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:54,720
Longan juice.

193
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,120
Longan juice. Same as you.

194
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:58,560
What do you want?

195
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:01,400
Lime soda.

196
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:04,200
No lime soda, only longan.
So two longan juices, okay?

197
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,080
- Hey.
- Phatee, what do you want?

198
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,000
I'll have an Americano.

199
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,280
Hot or iced?

200
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,360
Iced.

201
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,240
Light, medium, or dark roast?

202
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:15,400
- Dark roast.
- Okay.

203
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:19,200
Two longan juices. Americano…

204
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,520
Let's make it two.

205
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:22,920
Four drinks total.

206
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,080
Give me a sec.

207
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:31,400
TONHON

208
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,160
SAW

209
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:39,440
PJ

210
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,480
RANNE

211
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:48,640
PHATEE

212
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:53,080
<i>My world looks so dark and gloomy</i>

213
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:59,680
<i>When people stare, I just crumble</i>
<i>so I run away</i>

214
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:04,920
<i>Far from the crowd, just me</i>
<i>Oh, no</i>

215
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:09,440
<i>I try not to feel anything</i>

216
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:13,520
<i>But my heart never listens</i>

217
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:18,520
<i>I can't bear it</i>
<i>The sound of my heart's been so loud</i>

218
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:21,360
<i>Ever since you came</i>

219
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:25,760
<i>Too scared to say I love you</i>

220
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:29,240
<i>Just being near you is enough</i>

221
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:33,400
<i>I wouldn't dare to get closer to you</i>

222
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:39,720
<i>But what can I do? I'm in love with you</i>

223
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:43,680
<i>- Should I shout it out?</i>
<i>- I wouldn't dare</i>

224
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:46,280
<i>I wouldn't dare</i>

225
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:53,920
<i>Can I whisper it softly</i>
<i>To your ear instead?</i>

226
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:59,720
<i>I hate talking and making eye contact,</i>
<i>But I like it when you look over at me</i>

227
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:03,040
<i>I don't want to think or dream,</i>
<i>But every night there's only you</i>

228
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,240
<i>Didn't want to care,</i>
<i>scared it's getting real</i>

229
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:07,480
<i>But god, I really like you</i>

230
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,480
<i>Don't want love,</i>
<i>don't want any attachment</i>

231
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:11,280
<i>But when you smile,</i>
<i>my heart almost shatters</i>

232
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,080
<i>Oh-ooh-whoa-oh</i>

233
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,960
You really don't have to walk me back.

234
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,800
Well… it's dark.

235
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:27,520
It's dark?

236
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:33,360
I've walked alone for years.
Nothing's ever happened.

237
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,480
Just let me walk you back.

238
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,800
It's for the best.

239
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,720
Seriously.

240
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:45,160
I only said I'd carry your bag.

241
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:48,040
So you're not even going to
help me carry it?

242
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:52,680
You're the one
who said you wanted to carry it.

243
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,160
I'm just respecting that.

244
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,720
Come on, give it to me.

245
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,880
I was kidding.

246
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,560
I wasn't going to make you carry it.

247
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,599
I was just teasing you.

248
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,160
Okay.

249
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:16,040
So… which one's your car?

250
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:17,839
Here.

251
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,040
This one?

252
00:17:20,839 --> 00:17:22,359
Let me put my stuff away first.

253
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,560
What's wrong?

254
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,320
Nothing.

255
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,920
It's pretty late.

256
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,760
Want to stay at my place?

257
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,200
I don't mind.

258
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,720
But I do.

259
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:00,560
What's the problem?

260
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,080
I…

261
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,920
don't like sleeping
at other people's places.

262
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,160
I'll take you home.

263
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,840
Then I'll head back.

264
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,160
Okay. Let's do that.

265
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,640
Get in the car.

266
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,400
Come on, let's get in.

267
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:41,040
Oh. Rakkhun didn't come with you?

268
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,280
Why are you alone today, Vann?

269
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:45,120
He has things to do too.

270
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,440
Unlike you.

271
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:49,320
All you do is work out
and hang out with Yoyeh.

272
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:52,280
- Want these muscles to pound you, Vann?
- He's getting violent again. Look, Talay.

273
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,880
- Don't pick on him, Tangmo.
- Get off me!

274
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,080
Want some more?

275
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,840
Phatee. How are you?

276
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,080
Are you a singer yet?

277
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,400
Yeah.

278
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:06,160
I've seen you practicing hard every day.

279
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:09,120
I'm performing in two days.

280
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,160
Let me know if anyone wants to come.

281
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,240
Your debut stage?

282
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:18,120
My big bro is finally blowing up.

283
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,280
I'll take a photo to show off.

284
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,560
Damn, that's awesome.
I have an artist for a friend now.

285
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,440
I'm happy for you.

286
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,720
You finally achieved your dream.

287
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:32,160
The song isn't out yet,
so it doesn't count.

288
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,040
I don't know if it'll turn out well.

289
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,360
Hey.

290
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:38,720
What are you worried about?

291
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,160
You've worked this hard.

292
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:42,680
It has to turn out well.

293
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,680
Yeah.

294
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,480
You'll do great.

295
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,760
As for whether it'll blow up or not,

296
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:50,360
you can't control that.

297
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,560
Sometimes good stuff just doesn't blow up.

298
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,640
True.

299
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,760
But you've got me. What are you afraid of?

300
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,040
I'll get bots to boost your views.

301
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,560
Let's get you to ten million views.
Want that?

302
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,320
No need.

303
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,560
But I've seen the buzz on social media.

304
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:10,280
They're glued to it,
waiting for Phatee-Ranne moments.

305
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,440
I sing. I'm not selling moments.

306
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,000
The opportunity is here.

307
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:35,560
You have to seize it.

308
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,560
Which one do you mean?

309
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,680
I mean both.

310
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:44,080
Your dream and your love life.

311
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,560
If you let them slip away,

312
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:49,560
I won't know what else to say.

313
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,720
Come on, let's take a photo.

314
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,640
- Come on.
- Let's do it.

315
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:03,120
- Boost, boost, boost!
- So handsome.

316
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,680
- Hey.
- Hey, why aren't you smiling?

317
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:07,200
Let's take another one.

318
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:09,640
Smile a little.

319
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:11,760
Smile.

320
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,960
Ranne.

321
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:22,680
Vann.

322
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,800
Rakkhun, why are you wearing a suit?

323
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:29,480
You said we were going on a date,
so I dressed up a little.

324
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,480
You look cute in anything.

325
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,160
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

326
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,680
Wow.

327
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,120
This is a pretty big event.

328
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:44,760
I've never been to anything like this.

329
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:46,560
Of course.

330
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:49,840
It's super exclusive.
There are only 50 seats.

331
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,080
Really?

332
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,440
Let's take a photo with Phatee's standee.

333
00:21:59,560 --> 00:22:01,240
So handsome.

334
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,920
Here.

335
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,880
What's this?

336
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:10,760
Earplugs.

337
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:12,000
I brought them for you.

338
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:14,400
It's over 120 decibels inside.

339
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,680
I'm worried it could damage your eardrums.

340
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,920
Wow, you're being dramatic.

341
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,960
But… thanks.

342
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:26,160
You're the sweetest.

343
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,600
I'm your boyfriend.
I have to take care of you.

344
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:38,440
Want to take a photo with the standee?

345
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:40,520
- Sure.
- Let's go.

346
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,680
I'll take one with Ranne.

347
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,080
What about Phatee?

348
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,240
Phatee can wait.

349
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,440
Come see me when you're done.

350
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,200
Thanks, Fam.

351
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:03,920
<i>Meeting you means everything, everything</i>
<i>If you feel the same</i>

352
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,720
<i>Just tell me if you feel the same</i>

353
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:11,920
<i>Just tell me, oh-ooh-woah-oh</i>

354
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:15,560
<i>'Cause you mean everything, everything</i>
<i>If you feel--</i>

355
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,920
Who are you cursing at?

356
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:40,640
I've been watching you for a while.

357
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:42,520
Some asshole.

358
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:45,560
They keep trashing Phatee on X,
saying he only serves Ranne moments

359
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:46,720
and doesn't care about the band.

360
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:49,040
I've seen this account
do it several times.

361
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:50,680
They're gonna get it from me.

362
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:52,480
That's how it is when you're famous.

363
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:54,600
Some people like him, and some don't.

364
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,480
You can't go after every account.

365
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,680
I can. I can do it.

366
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,560
I could curse them out all day.

367
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:03,960
So these assholes know
how it feels to get cursed at.

368
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:05,440
They picked the wrong person to mess with.

369
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:08,520
You really haven't changed.

370
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,960
Let's go see Phatee.

371
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:16,040
What's with you?

372
00:24:16,720 --> 00:24:18,480
Didn't you say you'd watch the livestream?

373
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,600
I don't really want to go.

374
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:23,240
But the owner of this account
might be at the event.

375
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:24,960
So I can punch them in the face too.

376
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:28,360
How will you know who owns the account?

377
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:31,320
Right. True.

378
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:32,920
I'll figure it out later.

379
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:36,440
Anyway, I'll go film a prank on Phatee.

380
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:37,680
What about the club?

381
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:40,000
- Isn't there anyone to watch it?
- Nay will be back soon.

382
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:42,360
Come on. Let's hurry.

383
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,800
It's about to start.

384
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:50,560
Everyone.

385
00:24:51,280 --> 00:24:52,960
Just five more minutes.

386
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:58,360
Why did you bring me here?

387
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:01,360
I brought you here for research.

388
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:03,160
You can use it in your novel.

389
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,840
Try doing something new.

390
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:06,240
It'll get your brain going.

391
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:08,520
I don't really like it.

392
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:10,080
Too many people.

393
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,320
It's chaotic too.

394
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:13,920
Where are you going?

395
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:16,160
You're already here. Stay for a while.

396
00:25:16,760 --> 00:25:18,000
You're not that old yet.

397
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:21,560
Stop acting like an old man
who can't come up with ideas and

398
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:23,760
does nothing but drink and smoke all day.

399
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,400
Anything that clears my head

400
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:28,680
and gives me ideas, I'll do it.

401
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:30,640
But…

402
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:32,760
I can't handle this.

403
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:34,120
Too many people.

404
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:35,520
I'm dizzy.

405
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:38,320
Where are you going?

406
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:44,840
Then just look at me, like this.

407
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:46,400
Okay?

408
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:49,560
Are you tricking me into looking at you?

409
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:54,400
I don't need to.
You already like looking at me.

410
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:59,120
Don't be so full of yourself.

411
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:01,240
You're just the model for my character.

412
00:26:01,320 --> 00:26:03,320
Of course I have to look at you.
It helps me come up with ideas.

413
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:11,320
By the way…

414
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,680
do you like concerts like this?

415
00:26:15,120 --> 00:26:15,960
No.

416
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:17,840
I don't usually go to them.

417
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:19,920
But this is Phatee's debut concert.

418
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:23,840
The singer who likes to sing with
his back turned at The Crow Club.

419
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:29,440
I was wondering why he hasn't
been singing at the club lately.

420
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,360
Phatee wants to be an artist.

421
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:35,760
He's very talented.

422
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,000
The problem is,

423
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:38,720
he's a bit of an introvert.

424
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,480
More than a bit.

425
00:26:40,560 --> 00:26:43,800
He sings with his back turned
and ignores the audience.

426
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:45,920
That's true.

427
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:49,240
This is the first time he's dared to
pursue his dream.

428
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:51,680
So I wanted to come support him.

429
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:56,840
Let's go.

430
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:58,080
Let's go inside.

431
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:00,680
You go ahead.

432
00:27:00,760 --> 00:27:02,160
Just try it. Come on.

433
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:14,240
There you are.

434
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,120
Everyone's looking for you.

435
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,560
It's almost showtime.

436
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,400
Are you nervous?

437
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:30,160
Yeah.

438
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:34,080
Then…

439
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:38,200
try thinking of it like
singing at the club.

440
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:39,920
Would that help?

441
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:45,560
How is it the same?

442
00:27:46,720 --> 00:27:48,320
There are way more people here.

443
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:57,440
You don't… look nervous at all.

444
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:01,560
Who told you that?

445
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:26,280
Whoa.

446
00:28:27,120 --> 00:28:28,880
Your heart's beating so fast.

447
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:31,200
Are you going to die?

448
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:35,680
I told you.

449
00:28:49,920 --> 00:28:53,080
The last time I was onstage

450
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,920
was back in high school.

451
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:58,000
It was a long time ago.

452
00:28:58,080 --> 00:28:59,240
Back then,

453
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:01,520
I was this nervous too.

454
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:04,080
My heart nearly gave out.

455
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:10,960
But I still remember
exactly how it all felt.

456
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,840
The singing,

457
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:18,640
